    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d903">

                <pb facs="0991" n="899" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg899"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/8739</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-04T14:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 4, 1918, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 5.10 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8493. Your 6310, January 21, and my 8390, January 24. Mr. Balfour has shown me the declaration upholding
                    independence and integrity of Persia, made by British and French Governments,
                    and submitted for participation of our Government through British Ambassador at
                    Washington. This he thinks is all that can be done at present.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
